  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "CII hails GST Council's decriminalisation move as landmark tax reform",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/finance/news/cii-hails-gst-council-s-decriminalisation-move-as-landmark-tax-reform-126110100549_1.html",
      "description": "Industry body says proposed removal of GST arrest powers, higher prosecution thresholds and stronger taxpayer safeguards mark a major shift towards trust-based governance",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-01T11:47:23"
    },
    {
      "title": "GST decriminalisation decisions mark shift to trust-based governance: CII",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/gst-decriminalisation-decisions-mark-shift-to-trust-based-governance-cii-126110100421_1.html",
      "description": "Industry body CII on Sunday described the GST Council's decisions to decriminalise certain offences and rationalise enforcement powers as a significant institutional reform, saying the move marks a shift towards trust-based economic governance and offers a model for India's next generation of economic reforms.\nOn the decisions taken at the GST Council's October 8 meeting, CII said the consensus-driven approach showed how the Centre and states could work together on difficult reforms to improve the relationship between the government and businesses.\nCII Director General Chandrajit Banerjee said, \"The GST Council's decisions deserve special recognition as a landmark institutional reform. We deeply appreciate the leadership of Prime Minister Narendra Modi and Finance Minister Nirmala Sitharaman in advancing this transformation, and the constructive role of state governments in achieving consensus on an issue involving sensitive questions of enforcement, revenue protection and taxpayer .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-01T10:12:00"
    }
  ]
